  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Authorized copies of each score are available digitally and on paper, and the rehearsal notice identifies the required numbered pieces.\", \"decision\": \"How should singers obtain the music needed for rehearsal?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe organizer sends the numbered score list and digital copies before rehearsal, with matching paper copies available at arrival. Singers can prepare early while anyone who needs paper still receives the same music before singing begins.\nSection leaders assemble each singer’s requested paper or digital score set before the next rehearsal. A named contact checks the contents for that section, reducing missing pages without requiring everyone to use the same format.\nSingers collect the numbered scores from a shared catalog when the rehearsal notice appears and mark receipt on a list. Members control when they obtain music, while the organizer can identify gaps before the session starts."
    }
